Package: xlaport
Title: Run Exported XLA Programs (StableHLO) as R Functions
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Ben", "Traven", email = "ben.uzh@proton.me", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Ship kernels written in JAX (or anything else that emits StableHLO) inside an R
    package and call them as ordinary R functions, with no Python at runtime. Programs are
    compiled through 'pjrt' on the user's machine for the device in use and cached per session.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: jsonlite, pjrt (>= 0.6.0), stats
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
URL: https://github.com/btraven00/xlaport
BugReports: https://github.com/btraven00/xlaport/issues
Remotes: r-xla/pjrt
Additional_repositories: https://r-xla.r-universe.dev
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
